abstract = {This marks the 7th edition of the International Workshop on Engineering and Cybersecurity of Critical Systems (EnCyCriS) in conjunction with the 48th International Conference on Software Engineering (ICSE 2026).In each new edition the EnCyCriS workshop has gradually changed focus as society, technology and threat actors have developed and posed new challenges for critical infrastructures and systems. A challenge topic this year is the lack of readily deployable competences, methods, tools, and solutions, which should be considered a critical societal risk - versus AI and machine learning tools racing to fill that gap while at the same time introducing new challenges. It is very clear that the software engineering community, that continues to develop and maintain complex software to ensure security, robustness, and compliance throughout the system lifecycle, is a key player for safety and security.},
